## Candidate 3 amendments: T1 (P3, P4, P9)

Status: PROPOSED-UNFROZEN integration amendment of this imported copy (Lane P work package WP-T1; Order of 4 October 2026 decisions P3, P4, P9, Q15; design `qualification/candidate-3/P-LANE-DESIGN-V1.md` sections 1.a, 4, 5.1, 10). The exact rules are in `spec/BUILD8-TRADING-D1-LOCK-PACKET-V1.md`, section "Candidate 3 amendments: T1 (P3, P4, P9)"; this section records what changes in this system description. Later work packages (T2, T3, T4) append their own sections after this one.

* Validity (sections 3 and 5): every native trading operation carries the operation envelope instead of created/expiry heights (trading body version 2): a signed inclusion window, a finalized reference block and optional committed preconditions, all checked again at the actual inclusion height. A signed operation stays valid across head advances inside its window; retries never extend it. The DvP (section 11) no longer names an exact inclusion height; its transfer is recorded at the actual inclusion height and rights start at the next height.
* Destinations: a zero address is unrepresentable in every trading destination field; it is never a burn.
* Wallet history (section 11, "Current WalletBook authority validates each role, including wallet key rotation for historical addresses"): the payer of a trading operation may fund it from any authenticated generation of its own wallet lineage under the current key; unrelated wallets never count. The conditional payout recipient stays distinct from the fee funding.
* Treasury (section 12): reserve backing is enforced for every StateRoot, also for fees paid from the Treasury lineage; a Treasury at exactly its reserve needs an earlier top-up. The P6 authority rules are T3's amendment.

