## Candidate 3 amendments: T2 (P5)

Status: PROPOSED-UNFROZEN integration amendment of this imported copy (Lane P work package WP-T2; Order of 4 October 2026 decision P5 and Q17(a); Restart Order L64; design `qualification/candidate-3/P-LANE-DESIGN-V1.md` section 6). The exact rules are in `spec/BUILD8-TRADING-D1-LOCK-PACKET-V1.md`, section "Candidate 3 amendments: T2 (P5)"; this section records what changes in section 11.

* Commitment (section 11, "Both bind context, TradeID, ContractHash, LicenseID/current generation, exact parties, price, outputs, fee and inclusion rules"): both approvals additionally bind the sold License's remaining dividend rights (every live award account with share, remaining amount and claim sequence) and its assignment state (sequence, active Worker, pending assignment id), as two mandatory envelope preconditions. A sale without them is invalid.
* Validation point: the committed facts are compared after the sale block's epoch events (activations, award expiries and boundaries) and same-block Worker assignments, after earlier trades of the block and before any dividend claim. Any change (seller claim, expiry, an eligible new award, an assignment change) makes the sale stale: the block is invalid and the parties must review and sign again. Head advance alone, another License's events and an award for which the License is not eligible do not.
* Pending assignment (section 11, "It rejects pending Worker assignments"): replaced. The sale cancels the old owner's pending assignment if and only if the sale committed exactly that assignment; otherwise the sale is stale. The active Worker is detached as before.
* Rights: the License keeps its award accounts through the sale; nothing is recreated; a same-block seller claim of the sold License fails (claims run after trades) and a same-block buyer claim is valid.
